---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import LineChart from "../components/LineChart.astro";
import PeriodTable from "../components/PeriodTable.astro";
const sect = ["mining", "manufacturing", "electricity"];
const use = ["primary_goods", "capital_goods", "intermediate_goods", "infra_construction", "consumer_durables", "consumer_nondurables"];
---
<Base current="activity" title="Activity">
  <h1>Activity</h1>
  <p class="lede">What do the monthly indicators say about momentum before GDP comes out? Industrial production from MoSPI (Index of Industrial Production, base 2022-23).</p>

  <LineChart title="Industrial production growth, as published" subtitle="IIP, % change on a year earlier"
    lines={[{ id: "iip_general_growth", label: "IIP" }]} years={6} />
  <p class="chart-sub">Base 2022-23 from April 2023, base 2011-12 before; each value is the rate MoSPI published on that base. Recent months are quick estimates and are revised.</p>

  <h2>Industrial production by sector and use</h2>
  <PeriodTable heading="IIP, % y/y" n={6} rows={[
    { id: "iip_general_index", how: "yoy", label: "General" },
    ...sect.map((s) => ({ id: `iip_${s}_index`, how: "yoy", indent: true })),
    ...use.map((s) => ({ id: `iip_${s}_index`, how: "yoy", indent: true })),
  ]} />
  <p class="chart-sub">Computed from the published indices (site calculations), so they can differ from MoSPI's published growth by rounding. Sector rows are mining, manufacturing and electricity; the rest are use-based categories.</p>

  <LineChart title="Investment and consumer goods" subtitle="IIP use-based categories, % change on a year earlier"
    lines={[{ id: "iip_capital_goods_index", how: "yoy", label: "Capital goods" }, { id: "iip_infra_construction_index", how: "yoy", label: "Infrastructure/construction" },
            { id: "iip_consumer_durables_index", how: "yoy", label: "Consumer durables" }, { id: "iip_consumer_nondurables_index", how: "yoy", label: "Consumer non-durables" }]} years={3} />

  <h2>Core industries</h2>
  <LineChart title="Index of Core Industries" subtitle="% change on a year earlier"
    lines={[{ id: "core_overall_index", how: "yoy", label: "Core industries" }, { id: "iip_general_index", how: "yoy", label: "IIP" }]} years={2} />
  <PeriodTable heading="% y/y" n={6} rows={[
    { id: "core_overall_index", how: "yoy", label: "Overall" },
    ...["coal", "natural_gas", "crude_oil", "refinery", "fertilizers", "steel", "cement", "electricity", "iron_ore"]
      .map((k) => ({ id: `core_${k}_index`, how: "yoy", indent: true })),
  ]} />
  <p class="chart-sub">Office of the Economic Adviser, DPIIT; base 2022-23 (which adds iron ore to the eight traditional industries). Released about a week before IIP, so it is an early read on industry.</p>

  <h2>Electricity demand</h2>
  <div class="grid2">
    <LineChart title="Electricity demand met" subtitle="All-India energy met, million units per day, 7-day average" lines={[{ id: "power_energy_met", how: "7dma", label: "Energy met" }]} years={2} />
    <LineChart title="Electricity demand, change on a year earlier" subtitle="7-day average of energy met, % change on a year earlier" lines={[{ id: "power_energy_met", how: "7dma_yoy", label: "% y/y" }]} years={1} />
  </div>
  <p class="chart-sub">Grid-India daily Power Supply Position reports (operational SCADA data; excludes captive and rooftop generation). Daily data are noisy, so even the 7-day average moves sharply when festivals fall in different weeks from one year to the next, or with weather; compare monthly averages for the underlying trend. Shown with attribution; not offered for download until Grid-India's terms are checked.</p>

  <h2>Still to come on this page</h2>
  <p class="chart-sub"> GST and e-way bills, auto sales, fuel consumption, rail freight, air traffic, UPI, PMI headline. Checklist: docs/guidebook/05-pages/activity.md.</p>
</Base>
